  "id": "COMPOUND:18295 - PROTEIN:6293",
  "verbalization": "Decarine is implicated in the regulation of Dipeptidyl peptidase IX (DPPX) through a series of intermediate targets, including Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2, Rupicolin B, and Hydroxysaikosaponin c. These targets are all involved in the modulation of proteolytic activity, suggesting a potential role for Decarine in influencing DPPX function. The evidence indicates that Decarine may act as a modulator of the proteasome or related pathways, indirectly affecting DPPX through these intermediates. The consistent presence of Decarine as a target of Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2 across multiple paths supports a mechanism where Decarine influences the activity of this kinase, which in turn affects DPPX. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory relationship between Decarine and DPPX, mediated through a network of downstream targets.",
